{"id":"19.09.WaveBlocks","contentHtml":"<p>This project is a technical demo in which I implemented a unique game mechanic and the underlying technology from scratch.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The idea was to create a world that looks like solid ground but behaves like a liquid: the player can \"dive\" into it, digging tunnels, and be \"pushed\" to the surface with force.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2>Challenge</h2>\n<p>The key task was to create a <strong>high-performance for mobile devices, dynamically changeable 2D landscape</strong> on the GPU. It had to form <strong>smooth, organic \"caves\"</strong> and form the basis of a unique gameplay mechanic.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>Engineering Solution</h2>\n<p>The entire system is built on a single <code>HLSL</code> shader, which allowed achieving maximum performance.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Procedural Landscape on GPU:</strong> The entire visible mesh of the world is not thousands of objects, but a <strong>mathematically generated pattern inside the shader</strong>, which is rendered on a single flat surface.</li>\n<li><strong>Smooth Destruction:</strong> The player \"draws\" a trail in a <code>Render Texture</code>. The effect of smooth, organic edges is achieved in a fast and smart way: <strong><code>Bilinear</code> filtering</strong> in the <code>Render Texture</code> automatically smooths the edges of the drawn trail.</li>\n<li><strong>\"Diving\" Gameplay:</strong> This technology became the basis for the core mechanic: when holding, the player \"dives\" under the surface, and when releasing - is pushed out with force.</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>Outcome</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Optimization Achieved:</strong> The shader approach ensured <strong>maximum performance</strong> even on weak mobile devices.</li>\n<li><strong>Unique Gaming Experience:</strong> The technical solution formed the basis of interesting gameplay and a memorable visual style.</li>\n<li><strong>Key Competency:</strong> The project demonstrates my ability to <mark>solve complex optimization problems using GPU programming</mark> (<code>HLSL</code>, <code>Render Textures</code>) and create a unique gaming experience on this basis.</li>\n</ul>\n","published":true,"title":"Wave Blocks","date":"2019-09","type":"project","tagsArray":["Demo","Unity","C#","HLSL"],"heroVideo":["FAeJo1Vr7rA"],"shortDescription":"<p>Tech demo: <mark>High-performance 2D landscape</mark> where the world grid and smooth destruction are generated by a single shader.</p>\n","role":"solo","projectIcon":"/images/projects/19.09.WaveBlocks/icon.webp","cardBackground":"/images/projects/19.09.WaveBlocks/card.mp4?v=1765047006195","screenshots":[{"src":"/images/projects/19.09.WaveBlocks/screenshots/1.webp","width":1172,"height":924},{"src":"/images/projects/19.09.WaveBlocks/screenshots/2.webp","width":1172,"height":924},{"src":"/images/projects/19.09.WaveBlocks/screenshots/3.webp","width":1172,"height":924}]}